## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design multi-tenant data contracts, runtime validation, privacy masking, and governance in a real-time setting. Also probes trade-offs between Spark and Flink, plus testing strategies and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Runtime data contracts per tenant
- Per-tenant masking/redaction strategies
- GDPR deletion and data sovereignty
- Schema evolution in lakehouse (Iceberg/Parquet)
- Policy engine governance (e.g., OPA)
- Spark Structured Streaming vs Flink trade-offs
- Testing, monitoring, data quality

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo runtime contract check
function validateRecord(record, contract) {
  for (const field of Object.keys(contract.fields)) {
    if (!record.hasOwnProperty(field) && contract.fields[field].required) {
      throw new Error(`Missing required field ${field}`);
    }
  }
  // redaction example
  if (contract.mask) {
    for (const f of contract.mask) {
      if (record[f]) record[f] = "REDACTED";
    }
  }
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant masking guarantees in CI/CD?
- How would GDPR deletion requests propagate through streaming pipelines and downstream consumers?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design scalable, multi-tenant streaming graph pipelines with strict data contracts, lineage, and compliance controls in modern lakehouse setups.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming patterns: watermarking, lateness windows, fault tolerance
- Idempotent upserts in Iceberg with composite keys (tenant/device/neighbor)
- Schema evolution for nested attributes and backward compatibility
- Per-record lineage and auditability; GDPR delete handling via tombstones
- Multi-tenant isolation, access controls, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo upsert for edge state
function upsertEdge(existing, incoming) {
  const key = `${incoming.tenant_id}:${incoming.device_id}:${incoming.neighbor_id}`;
  if (!existing || existing.version < incoming.version) return incoming;
  return existing;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test late-arrival handling across tenants?
- What monitoring would you implement to detect cross-tenant data leakage or drift?
